    </section>

    <!-- Why this matters -->
    <section class="section gh-why">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="section-label">Why this matters for you</span>
        <h2 class="headline-md">A platform you can trust the boring parts of.</h2>
        <p>
          Most "you'll never see this" parts of running software online are
          where the danger lives — unreviewed changes, untested deploys,
          forgotten secrets, surprise dependency upgrades, "we'll fix it
          later" branches. Pagayo doesn't have those, because GitHub
          doesn't let it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every change goes through the same path. Every deploy ends with
          a green check and a tag you can roll back to. Every secret
          lives somewhere we can audit. The discipline is built into the
          tools, not into anyone's memory — which is what makes it
          possible to keep shipping every week, indefinitely, with one
          person at the keyboard and a small army of agents helping out.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <FinalCta />
